voting power to control significant corporate actions. Bit Digital&#8217;s interests may be different from or conflict with our interests
or the interests of our other shareholders and noteholders.</i></span></p><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-weight: bold;"><i>&#160;</i></span></p><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">Bit Digital owned approximately
70.5% of the voting power of our issued and outstanding Ordinary Shares as of December 31, 2025. As a result of its ownership, Bit Digital
